 The list of discovered PuppetDB targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.puppetdbSDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
 
+## scaleway_sd_configs
+
+Scaleway SD configuration discovers scrape targets from [Scaleway](https://www.scaleway.com/en/) Instances.
+
+Configuration example:
+
+```yaml
+scrape_configs:
+- job_name: scaleway
+  scaleway_sd_configs:
+
+    # zone is the Scaleway zone to discover Instances from (mandatory).
+    # See: https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/api/#regions-and-zones
+  - zone: "fr-par-1"
+
+    # secret_key is the Scaleway API secret key to use for authentication (mandatory).
+    # It is sent as the `X-Auth-Token` HTTP header in every API request during service discovery.
+    # See: https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/identity-and-access-management/iam/how-to/create-api-keys/
+    secret_key: "..."
+
+    # Scaleway provides query arguments to filter instances. All of them are optional.
+    # See: https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/api/instance/#path-servers-list-servers
+
+    # project is an optional query argument to filter instances by project id.
+    #
+    # project: "..."
+
+    # organization is an optional query argument to filter instances by organization id.
+    #
+    # organization: "..."
+
+    # tags is an optional list of tags to filter instances by.
+    #
+    # tags: ["...", "..."]
+
+    # api_url is the Scaleway API server to query.
+    # By default, https://api.scaleway.com is used.
+    #
+    # api_url: "..."
+
+    # port is an optional port to scrape metrics from.
+    # By default, port 80 is used.
+    #
+    # port: ...
+
+    # Additional HTTP API client options can be specified here.
+    # See https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#http-api-client-options
+```
+
+Each discovered target has an [`__address__`](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/#how-to-modify-scrape-urls-in-targets) label set
+to `<IP>:<port>`, where `<IP>` is the discovered instance's public IP address, or its private IP address if no public IP is assigned,
+and `<port>` is the port from the `scaleway_sd_configs` (default port is `80`).
+
+The following meta labels are available on discovered targets during [relabeling](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/):
+
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_boot_type`: the boot type used by the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_hostname`: the hostname of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_id`: the unique ID of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_image_id`: the ID of the image the instance was booted from, if any.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_image_name`: the name of the image the instance was booted from, if any.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_name`: the name of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_organization_id`: the ID of the organization the instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_private_ipv4`: the private IPv4 address of the instance, if any.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_project_id`: the ID of the project the instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv4`: the public IPv4 address of the instance, if any.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_status`: the instance status, which could be `running`, `stopped`, `stopped in place`, `starting`, `stopping` or `locked`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_tags`: comma-separated list of tags assigned to the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_type`: the [commercial type](https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/api/instance/#path-instance-types-list-instance-types) of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_zone`: the zone the instance was discovered in.
+
+The list of discovered Scaleway targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.scalewaySDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
+
 ## static_configs
 
 A static config allows specifying a list of targets and a common label set for them.
